# A function of its callee's own color inside a non-empty array the call returns
# (`[T]+`), at a call that makes the color bounded (Type System ch. 4: a function that
# takes a closure takes the closure's color). `NamedRecolored` meets `Prelude.NonEmpty`,
# the array's type as the checker gives it, which no declaration names. Reaches the
# internal error "a prismc bug: the type `Prelude.NonEmpty` of a value a call returns,
# which nothing declares" on prismc-r27 (probe rc4 of fin-g).
# Written by Claude (t2, the prismc run), 12 November 2026; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

Both: u fn (u fn Nat -> Nat) -> [u fn Nat -> Nat]+
fn Both F = [[F, F]]+

Twice: fn Nat -> Nat
fn Twice k:
    let fs = Both (\|n| n + 1)
    Fold fs, k, \|acc, F| F acc

@page: @unit
@page:
    Ui.Label($text=$"{Twice 5}")                                 # 0
